{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they encamped in Rephidim, and there was no water.</b> According to the Sages, of blessed memory (Bekhorot 5a), 'Rephidim' means nothing other than slackening of hands, from the Torah. The verse intends to say: when they slackened their hands from the Torah, which is compared to water — therefore HaShem also withheld water from them, measure for measure."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:04.651331866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}